# The build context, kept to what the image actually needs.
#
# Without this it is over four gigabytes: `node_modules` and the Rust `target`
# directory alone are 4.3GB, and copying a host-built `node_modules` into a
# Linux image is a good way to get native modules compiled for the wrong
# platform. Everything below is either rebuilt inside the image or has no
# business in it.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.venv
core/.venv

# Rust build output for the desktop shell, which the container never runs.
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target
apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen

.git
.github
# No Markdown is needed to build: pyproject declares no readme.
*.md

# Never build a journal, a key, or a database into an image.
.env
**/.tilt
